{"code":200,"message":"OK","tweet":{"url":"https://x.com/lukaivanovic/status/2079178687409279303","id":"2079178687409279303","text":"","raw_text":{"text":"https://t.co/SaQZQxUQau","display_text_range":[0,23],"facets":[]},"author":{"screen_name":"lukaivanovic","url":"https://x.com/lukaivanovic","id":"2835133671","followers":1306,"following":1388,"likes":7530,"media_count":68,"name":"luka","description":"mots @lovable prev @daytonaio @tryprofound @akkiohq @weweb_io","raw_description":{"text":"mots @lovable prev @daytonaio @tryprofound @akkiohq @weweb_io","facets":[]},"location":"Europe","banner_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/2835133671/1767692188","avatar_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2011449711153012736/OmrSepuN_200x200.jpg","joined":"Fri Oct 17 15:48:05 +0000 2014","protected":false,"website":{"url":"https://ivanovicluka.co","display_url":"ivanovicluka.co"},"verification":{"verified":true,"verified_at":null,"type":"individual"},"avatar_color":null},"replies":5,"retweets":10,"likes":170,"bookmarks":461,"quotes":3,"created_at":"Mon Jul 20 12:16:43 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1784549803,"possibly_sensitive":false,"views":48651,"is_note_tweet":false,"community_note":null,"lang":null,"replying_to":null,"replying_to_status":null,"source":"Twitter Web App","article":{"created_at":"2026-07-20T12:16:42.000Z","modified_at":"2026-07-20T12:16:42.000Z","id":"2075501669991817216","title":"How to create your own design tool","preview_text":"The post below got a lot of attention so I'm posting a full guide on how I came to this setup.\n \n \nLike many others, I've replaced design tools with agents in my day to day work. They allow me to","cover_media":{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAFCgABHNHdsuyWEAAKAAIAAAAAqPy05wAA","media_id":"2076684663737683968","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiImage","color_info":{"palette":[{"percentage":76.5,"rgb":{"blue":245,"green":245,"red":245}},{"percentage":12.18,"rgb":{"blue":56,"green":5,"red":221}},{"percentage":4.29,"rgb":{"blue":182,"green":43,"red":233}},{"percentage":1.87,"rgb":{"blue":78,"green":0,"red":221}},{"percentage":1.5,"rgb":{"blue":222,"green":110,"red":52}}]},"original_img_height":1122,"original_img_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HNHdsuyWEAAulib.jpg","original_img_width":2805},"media_key":"3_2076684663737683968"},"content":{"blocks":[{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"am86n","text":"The post below got a lot of attention so I'm posting a full guide on how I came to this setup.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":0,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"1m98h","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":1,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"eada2","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"7lnt5","text":"Like many others, I've replaced design tools with agents in my day to day work. They allow me to design and ship features from start to finish, while not having to worry about maintaining a Figma design system or spending time sketching states and prototypes.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"bejq9","text":"Newer tools like Paper made real improvements, keeping the iteration speed while accepting code as an equal tenet. I can simply ask my agent to pull up a component from the codebase and then quickly iterate on it. Worth mentioning is Paper's Chrome extension as well, which allows you to pull up exact screens to the canvas.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"fbrjl","text":"The problem arises once you try to make structural changes to those. Let's say I'm working on a chat composer and want to make a few mockups. I would take take a snapshot of my product, pull it up in a design tool and ask for some changes. At that point, the agent sees only a huge list of unnamed layers and the word composer is an unknown concept. More issues arise when I want to use my design system which I don't want to set up in a design tool.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"8rmrm","text":"Inspired by the new tools and guided by problems, I've decided to build a design tool of my own.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":2,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6h11v","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"818c5","text":"Chapter 1: Getting your layers","type":"header-two"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":3,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"ae12o","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"aim4","text":"Frontend states can get very complicated with logic flowing deep and wide which means adding or changing something would involve huge code changes. The same applies for mocking up or using placeholder data instead of your backend.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"7de57","text":"That's why we take a book out of the current design tools and target DOM elements which map more cleanly to the concept of layers. ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"5urc1","text":"Easiest way to allow your agent to snapshot the DOM is by installing the Chrome MCP or using a headless Playwright browser. To install the Chrome MCP, add the following to your MCP config:","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":4,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"dr6os","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"a5dvl","text":"After that, it's as easy as using this prompt in your agent to get the snapshot of any page or component:","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":5,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"ddorh","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":6,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"43b4c","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6r3kv","text":"Chapter 2: Provide context","type":"header-two"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":7,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"9pcrq","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"4b1bd","text":"To solve the context problem design tools struggle with, we need to provide more context to our exported layers. That's why we add important information like the component name, location in the codebase and it's kind for nested components.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"amtnn","text":"Here's an example prompt to get started on a Vite/Next project, but it will work for any framework:","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":8,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"5isi4","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"c1h63","text":"The exported layer of a sample card will look like this now:","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":9,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"5timj","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":10,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"8ddmn","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"1vus8","text":"Chapter 3: Create your artboards","type":"header-two"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":11,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"du9uq","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"cs4f1","text":"Now it's time to start designing and for that we need to be able to create our artboards. We create a script that does the following:","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"bnhmn","text":"Captures a page or a component into layers","type":"ordered-list-item"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"brpic","text":"Creates a new URL with the captured design","type":"ordered-list-item"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"fsa5k","text":"Example prompt to create yours:","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":12,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"32cqv","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":13,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"4q7ie","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"8o2i","text":"Chapter 4: Go wild","type":"header-two"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":14,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"e1bj4","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6u0ia","text":"With our artboard ready, the next step is making whatever you need. You can mock up the data, create animations, add shaders or 3d to your ","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"6elen","text":"Use helpers like Tweakpane, DialKit, Agentation and more to preserve some of the finer control of your designs or animations.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":15,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"2vfkq","text":" ","type":"atomic"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"fg7oi","text":"Additional: Editing and exporting videos","type":"header-two"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"22v8r","text":"Once a scene feels right, we can screen record and edit in a video editing software or you can prompt your agent to set up a Remotion scene to add effects and remove.","type":"unstyled"},{"data":{},"entityRanges":[{"key":16,"length":1,"offset":0}],"inlineStyleRanges":[],"key":"echf7","text":" ","type":"atomic"}],"entityMap":[{"key":"12","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"b0b285f3-adbd-4763-9ee3-abeaf77d2b5c","markdown":"```plaintext\nWrite a CLI script (e.g. pnpm design:extract route --input capture.json --name hero-card) that generates a new file-based route under /design/<name> which renders sanitized captured HTML with no app header, nav, or padding wrapper — just the isolated component.\n```"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"MARKDOWN"}},{"key":"8","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"f46f5720-35f3-4e46-90b7-8aaa809c0c03","markdown":"```plaintext\nAdd a Vite plugin (or Next SWC plugin) that tags every JSX host element with data-lv-source (file:line), data-lv-owner (nearest named component), and data-lv-kind (host tag) during dev builds only, gated behind an env flag like LOVABLE_DOM_METADATA=true.\n```"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"MARKDOWN"}},{"key":"4","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"15a9a9ca-db0a-4744-994b-d917ca4cb09a","markdown":"```json\n{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"chrome-devtools\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"-y\", \"chrome-devtools-mcp@latest\"]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"MARKDOWN"}},{"key":"15","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"c08c0621-ba11-4c58-824e-4c4fe7fb39f3"},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"DIVIDER"}},{"key":"11","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"2bfe3ad4-c1d9-49a7-a938-33bc24bc3e8f","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"8","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2078126852254650368"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"9","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"8b8549e3-ba98-4bc0-8ab4-b932bd32f94b","markdown":"```htmlbars\n<div\n  data-lv-source=\"src/components/PricingCard.tsx:42\"\n  data-lv-owner=\"PricingCard\"\n  data-lv-kind=\"div\"\n  class=\"rounded-xl border p-6\"\n>\n  ...\n</div>\n```"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"MARKDOWN"}},{"key":"13","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"c49197a5-42bd-4089-82ae-f26be7541a32"},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"DIVIDER"}},{"key":"16","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"faaa6c95-7134-4695-b0c6-6841c2f7d4d6","markdown":"```plaintext\nInstall Remotion package and transform our route into an exportable artifact with support for adding vignette effects, motion blur or radial blur on the edges.\n```"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"MARKDOWN"}},{"key":"5","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"34c95550-e887-4ccc-a4e1-8a1de4534820","markdown":"```plaintext\nOpen <url> in the browser, set viewport to 1440x900, take a DOM snapshot of the dashboard page.\n```"},"mutability":"Mutable","type":"MARKDOWN"}},{"key":"10","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"020b7ae2-db7f-408c-8a6b-35f16f8d7097"},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"DIVIDER"}},{"key":"6","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"bb9ae31a-6b93-4ef8-ab33-86031b2a48e4"},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"DIVIDER"}},{"key":"1","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"51ae3673-2ed2-4cd6-95ad-1d63e99ffbfb","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"5","mediaCategory":"AmplifyVideo","mediaId":"2079178330822062080"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"14","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"7b6d9363-e986-40c0-8b46-bf6a2ae07cf9","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"10","mediaCategory":"AmplifyVideo","mediaId":"2078127169327230976"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"0","value":{"data":{"tweetId":"2067242140590076198"},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"TWEET"}},{"key":"2","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"4b4b73d0-e0e0-4eaa-9c9a-af5244816c82"},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"DIVIDER"}},{"key":"7","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"775b3f16-3c47-4f15-a255-e247bdb78f65","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"5","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2078126332597186560"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}},{"key":"3","value":{"data":{"entityKey":"d9eb060c-1476-4a00-858f-aefc78769176","mediaItems":[{"localMediaId":"2","mediaCategory":"DraftTweetImage","mediaId":"2078124186023739392"}]},"mutability":"Immutable","type":"MEDIA"}}]},"media_entities":[{"id":"QXBpTWVkaWE6DAAFCgABHNb845zXMAAKAAIAAAAAqPy05wAA","media_id":"2078126332597186560","media_info":{"__typename":"ApiImage","color_info":{"palette":[{"percentage":58.37,"rgb":{"blue":29,"green":31,"red":31}},{"percentage":16.61,"rgb